@startuml allocation_fleet_orchestration
title Allocation, Fleet, and Orchestration Layers\nClass structure + numbered arrows tracing the render flow\n(arrow color = source module; numbers = order in the render lifecycle)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam BackgroundColor white
skinparam classBackgroundColor #fafafa
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #ffffd0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype polyline

' ============================================================
' Layer 1 -- API
' ============================================================
package "API (api/routers)" <<Frame>> #d4e3fc {
    class JobsRouter {
        + agent_failure(job_id, error)
        + register_outputs(job_id, files)
        + update_status(job_id, payload)
        + heartbeat(job_id, payload)
        + next_for_machine(machine_id)
        + retry(job_id)
    }
    class RenderGroupsRouter {
        + confirm_upload(group_id, payload)
        + rerender(group_id, payload)
        + cancel(group_id)
    }
    class MachinesRouter {
        + register(payload)
        + heartbeat(machine_id)
        + set_available(machine_id)
        + set_idle(machine_id)
    }
    class InternalRouter {
        + report_orphan(job_id, payload)
    }
}

' ============================================================
' Layer 2 -- Service
' ============================================================
package "Service (services)" <<Frame>> #fed7aa {
    class RenderGroupService {
        + confirm_upload()
        + rerender()
        + cancel()
    }
    class JobService {
        + next_for_machine(machine_id)
        + register_outputs(job_id, files)
        + notify_completion(job_id)
        + heartbeat(job_id, ...)
        + update_status(...)
    }
    class MachineService {
        + register(payload, user_id)
        + heartbeat(machine_id)
        + set_available(machine_id)
        + set_idle(machine_id)
    }

    note right of RenderGroupService #ddffdd
      Engine resolution boundary:
      confirm_upload + rerender resolve
      engine = override OR snapshot, then
      WRITE it back into render_overrides
      BEFORE serializing to JSON.
      Single source of truth for both
      initial dispatch AND retry.
    end note

    note right of JobService #ddffdd
      register_outputs returns 200 to the
      worker IMMEDIATELY after the DB merge,
      then schedules notify_completion as a
      FastAPI BackgroundTask.  When the
      verified output_files count reaches
      total_frames, success_notifier fires
      ->  CallbackRouter.route(SUCCESS).
      Workers cannot self-report "done";
      data IS the success signal.
    end note

    note right of MachineService #ddffdd
      heartbeat() writes Redis (sorted set
      machines:alive) -- NO Postgres write.
      set_idle clears the Redis entry.
      machines.last_seen_at column kept for
      informational reads only, set on
      register / set_available transitions.
    end note
}

' ============================================================
' Layer 3 -- Orchestration
' ============================================================
package "Orchestration (orchestrator)" <<Frame>> #ddd6fe {
    class RenderOrchestrator <<facade>> {
        + plan(engine, ...)
        + execute(render_overrides_json, ...)
        + on_job_failed(job_id, error)
        + on_job_succeeded(job_id)
        + on_job_running(job_id)
        + cancel_group(group_id)
        + retry_chunk_manually(job_id)
    }

    class RenderLifecycle {
        + plan(engine, ...)
        + start_render(...)
        + handle_chunk_failed(job_id, error)
        + handle_chunk_succeeded(job_id)
        + retry_chunk_manually(job_id)
        + cancel_render(group_id)
        + reconcile_group_status(group_id)
        - _try_dispatch_retry(job_id, error)
    }

    class DispatchCoordinator {
        + enqueue_and_flush(group_id, tasks, ctx)
        + drain_for_fleet(fleet)
        - _dispatch_queue_item(item)
    }

    class Dispatcher {
        + dispatch_one(task, context, job_id)
    }

    class LifecycleFramesDeduplication {
        + compute_remaining_for_chunk(group_id, chunk_index)
        + compute_total_rendered(jobs)
    }

    note right of RenderLifecycle #ddffdd
      Owner of group-level state.
      Decisions live here:
        - retry attempt limit + anti-affinity
        - eager strategy.cancel + stop_monitoring
          on chunk-success (closes Vast
          runtype=args auto-restart window,
          stops Modal billing immediately)
        - community machine lock release on
          terminal transitions
      Grunt computation delegated to
      LifecycleFramesDeduplication and
      DispatchCoordinator.
    end note

    note right of LifecycleFramesDeduplication #ddffdd
      Authoritative rendered-frame
      accounting via SET-UNION of
      output_files across sibling
      attempts of a chunk.

      Used by:
        retry paths -> remaining frame range
                       (handles parallel-dispatch
                        races correctly)
        group rollup -> total_rendered count
                       (no double-count when two
                        workers rendered same frame)
    end note
}

' ============================================================
' Layer 4 -- Callbacks
' ============================================================
package "Callbacks (callbacks)" <<Frame>> #cffafe {
    class CallbackRouter {
        + route(job_id, outcome, error?)
    }

    class SuccessHandler {
        + handle(job_id, group_id)
    }
    class FailureHandler {
        + handle(job_id, error)
    }

    note right of CallbackRouter #ddffdd
      Single funnel for ALL outcome events.
      is_job_terminal short-circuit guard
      collapses duplicate signals to a
      single transition.

      Sources of SUCCESS (one path):
        JobService.register_outputs ->
          notify_completion -> here

      Sources of FAILURE (five paths,
      ALL routed through here):
        - JobsRouter.agent_failure (community)
        - InternalRouter.report_orphan (cron)
        - VastInstanceMonitor (_on_failure)
        - ModalJobMonitor (_on_failure)
        - CommunityMonitor (group-terminal,
          machine-offline, pre-render stall)

      No caller reaches RenderOrchestrator
      .on_job_failed directly anymore.
    end note
}

' ============================================================
' Layer 5 -- Allocation
' ============================================================
package "Allocation (orchestrator/allocation)" <<Frame>> #fecaca {
    interface FrameAllocator <<protocol>> {
        + allocate_initial(...)
        + allocate_retry(chunk_request, resources)
    }

    class DefaultAllocationStrategy
    class EconomyAllocationStrategy
    class FastRenderAllocationStrategy

    DefaultAllocationStrategy     -[#dc2626,dashed]-|> FrameAllocator
    EconomyAllocationStrategy     -[#dc2626,dashed]-|> FrameAllocator
    FastRenderAllocationStrategy  -[#dc2626,dashed]-|> FrameAllocator

    class ChunkRequest <<dataclass>> {
        + group_id, chunk_index
        + frame_start, frame_end
        + total_frames, attempt
        + excluded_machine_ids
        + excluded_serverless_capabilities
        + file_size_bytes
        + engine
    }

    class ValidationContext <<dataclass>> {
        + engine
    }

    interface TargetValidator <<protocol>> {
        + is_valid(target, ctx)
    }

    class EngineCompatibilityValidator
    EngineCompatibilityValidator -[#dc2626,dashed]-|> TargetValidator

    note right of EngineCompatibilityValidator #ddffdd
      Strict: raises ValueError when
      ctx.engine is None.

      Gates EEVEE off:
        modal_serverless (no graphics caps)
        community (WSL2 + NVCT ships only
          compute libs to containers)
      Allows: vast_serverless
    end note
}

' ============================================================
' Layer 5b -- Stall Detection
' ============================================================
package "Stall Detection (fleets/shared/pre_render_stall_detector)" <<Frame>> #fef3c7 {
    interface IPreRenderStallDetector <<protocol>> {
        + evaluate(window, job_age_sec) : StallReason | None
    }

    class PreRenderStallDetector {
        + evaluate(window, job_age_sec)
    }

    class PreRenderStallDetectorBuilder <<builder>> {
        + with_cpu_stall(threshold, window, rss_noise)
        + with_bytes_stall(stall_sec)
        + with_download_ceiling(secs_per_gb, min, max)
        + with_hard_ceiling(max_sec)
        + build() : IPreRenderStallDetector
    }

    interface StallRule <<protocol>> {
        + evaluate(window, job_age_sec) : StallReason | None
    }

    class CpuStallRule
    class BytesStallRule
    class DownloadCeilingRule
    class HardCeilingRule

    class HeartbeatWindow <<value object>> {
        + samples : list[Heartbeat]
        + within_last(sec)
        + oldest_in_phase(phase)
    }
    class StallReason <<dataclass>> {
        + rule, message
    }

    PreRenderStallDetector       -[#a16207,dashed]-|> IPreRenderStallDetector
    PreRenderStallDetectorBuilder -[#a16207]-> PreRenderStallDetector : builds
    CpuStallRule                 -[#a16207,dashed]-|> StallRule
    BytesStallRule               -[#a16207,dashed]-|> StallRule
    DownloadCeilingRule          -[#a16207,dashed]-|> StallRule
    HardCeilingRule              -[#a16207,dashed]-|> StallRule
    PreRenderStallDetector       -[#a16207]-> StallRule : runs rules in order,\nfirst match returns

    note right of PreRenderStallDetectorBuilder #ddffdd
      Stateless across jobs.  Bootstrap
      registers a 0-arg factory:
        _make_pre_render_stall_detector()
      Per-fleet behaviour:
        Vast / Modal: factory called per
          start_monitoring -- one detector
          per active job, lives with the
          monitor thread.
        Community: ONE detector built at
          init, reused across all jobs
          (stateless w.r.t. job_id; takes
          window + age as inputs).

      Reads heartbeat sliding window from
      Redis (HeartbeatRepository.get_recent),
      not in-memory state -- recovery
      reattaches monitors with a fresh
      detector and the existing window.
    end note

    note right of CpuStallRule #ffe4e6
      Currently DISABLED in the bootstrap
      factory.  Worker handler.py idles at
      ~0% CPU (Blender does the work in a
      child process).  Re-enable once the
      worker's ProcessSampler walks
      children.
    end note
}

' ============================================================
' Layer 6 -- Fleet
' ============================================================
package "Fleet (fleets)" <<Frame>> #bbf7d0 {
    class FleetRegistry {
        + register(strategy)
        + get(fleet)
    }

    interface IFleetStrategy <<protocol>> {
        + dispatch(task, context, job_id)
        + cancel(provider_job_id)
        + stop_monitoring(job_id)
        + provider_job_id_from_job(job)
    }

    package "vast" <<Frame>> #d1fae5 {
        class VastFleetStrategy
        class VastClient
        class VastCallbackHandler
        class VastInstanceMonitor
        class VastRecovery
    }

    package "modal" <<Frame>> #d1fae5 {
        class ModalFleetStrategy
        class ModalClient
        class ModalCallbackHandler
        class ModalJobMonitor
        class ModalRecovery
    }

    package "community" <<Frame>> #d1fae5 {
        class CommunityStrategy
        class CommunityMonitor
    }

    VastFleetStrategy      -[#16a34a,dashed]-|> IFleetStrategy
    ModalFleetStrategy     -[#16a34a,dashed]-|> IFleetStrategy
    CommunityStrategy      -[#16a34a,dashed]-|> IFleetStrategy

    note right of VastClient #ddffdd
      Encodes render_overrides_json -> base64
      ONLY at the wire boundary (RENDER_OVERRIDES_B64
      env var).  Same pattern in modal/client.py.
    end note

    note right of CommunityStrategy
      No provider API call. Dispatch is
      a JobRepository insert -- the DB row
      IS the message to the agent, which
      polls /jobs/next-for-machine and
      claims it via claim_next_for_machine.
    end note

    note right of CommunityMonitor #ddffdd
      Two thresholds:
        stale_seconds (~30s) -- per-job
          machine-offline detection.
        demote_seconds (~90s) -- "agent
          crashed" threshold for flipping
          Postgres status -> idle.

      Per-tick:
        - check group-terminal cascades
        - check machine-offline (Redis alive_ids)
        - check pre-render stall (heartbeat window)
        - demote ghost machines (status='available'
          but absent from wide alive_ids window)
        - prune stale Redis entries
    end note
}

' ============================================================
' Layer 7 -- Repositories
' ============================================================
package "Repositories (repositories)" <<Frame>> #e5e7eb {
    class JobRepository {
        --table jobs--
        + claim_next_for_machine
        + create / mark_done / mark_failed
        + merge_output_files
        + get_raw_by_id / get_raw_by_group
    }
    class MachineRepository {
        --table machines--
        + set_processing
        + set_available
        + get_available_community
        + demote_ghosts(alive_ids)
    }
    class RenderGroupRepository {
        --table render_groups--
        + get_by_id
        + full_update
    }
    class DispatchQueueRepository {
        --table dispatch_queue--
        + enqueue / dequeue / drain
    }
    class InProgressChunkRepository {
        --in-memory ledger--
        + claim_or_replace
        + release / current_job_for
    }
    class HeartbeatRepository {
        --Redis: job liveness--
        + record(job_id, telemetry)
        + get_recent(job_id)
    }
    class MachineHeartbeatRepository {
        --Redis: machine liveness--
        + record(machine_id)
        + alive_ids(stale_seconds)
        + clear(machine_id)
        + prune_stale(stale_seconds)
    }
    class ProgressRepository {
        --Redis: per-job progress--
        + record / get
    }

    note right of JobRepository #ddffdd
      claim_next_for_machine atomically
      flips machines.status -> 'processing'
      alongside the job claim.  Liveness
      lives in Redis (MachineHeartbeatRepository);
      no last_seen_at write here.
    end note

    note right of MachineRepository #ddffdd
      get_available_community returns
      status='available' rows only;
      liveness intersect happens in
      bootstrap._resource_picker against
      MachineHeartbeatRepository.alive_ids.
      demote_ghosts is the periodic
      reconciler called by CommunityMonitor.
    end note

    note right of MachineHeartbeatRepository #ddffdd
      Single Redis sorted set
      machines:alive (member=machine_id,
      score=unix_ts).  ZRANGEBYSCORE
      returns the alive cohort in O(log N).
      Replaces the per-heartbeat Postgres
      UPDATE that hit Neon connection-died-
      mid-request errors.
    end note
}

' ============================================================
' Cross-layer dependencies (arrow color = source module)
' Numbered arrows trace the render lifecycle in order.
' ============================================================

' --- 1. User submits a render ---
RenderGroupsRouter   -[#2563eb]-> RenderGroupService    : 1. confirm_upload\nor rerender or cancel
RenderGroupService   -[#f97316]-> RenderOrchestrator    : 2. plan(engine, heaviness, tier)\n   then execute(tasks, render_overrides_json)

' --- 2. Plan: pick a strategy and emit PlannedTask list ---
RenderOrchestrator   *-[#7c3aed]- RenderLifecycle       : facade
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed,dashed]-> FrameAllocator : 3. pick Default / FastRender / Economy\n   per heaviness + tier
FrameAllocator       -[#dc2626,dashed]-> ValidationContext : 4. per-allocation engine ctx
FrameAllocator       -[#dc2626,dashed]-> TargetValidator   : 5. filter eligible targets
ChunkRequest         -[#dc2626,dashed]-> ValidationContext : engine flows from request

' --- 3. Execute: queue + dispatch per chunk ---
RenderLifecycle      *-[#7c3aed]- DispatchCoordinator   : 6. enqueue_and_flush\n   (per-fleet cap)
DispatchCoordinator  -[#7c3aed]-> DispatchQueueRepository : 7. enqueue / dequeue
DispatchCoordinator  -[#7c3aed]-> InProgressChunkRepository : 8. claim_or_replace ledger
DispatchCoordinator  *-[#7c3aed]- Dispatcher
Dispatcher           -[#7c3aed]-> FleetRegistry         : 9. strategy lookup by fleet

VastFleetStrategy    -[#16a34a]-> VastClient            : 10a. create instance
VastFleetStrategy    -[#16a34a]-> VastCallbackHandler   : 10b. start per-job monitor
ModalFleetStrategy   -[#16a34a]-> ModalClient           : 10a. spawn FunctionCall
ModalFleetStrategy   -[#16a34a]-> ModalCallbackHandler  : 10b. start per-job monitor
CommunityStrategy    -[#16a34a]-> JobRepository         : 10. INSERT pending job\n     (agent polls + claims)

VastFleetStrategy    -[#16a34a]-> JobRepository         : 11. create job row\n     status='pending'
ModalFleetStrategy   -[#16a34a]-> JobRepository         : 11. create job row\n     status='pending'
VastCallbackHandler  *-[#16a34a]- VastInstanceMonitor   : owns thread per job
ModalCallbackHandler *-[#16a34a]- ModalJobMonitor       : owns thread per job

' --- 4. Worker telemetry: heartbeat, progress, register-outputs ---
JobsRouter           -[#2563eb]-> JobService            : 12. heartbeat / register-outputs / progress
JobService           -[#f97316]-> HeartbeatRepository   : 13a. record (Redis sliding window)
JobService           -[#f97316]-> ProgressRepository    : 13b. progress counter (Redis)
JobService           -[#f97316]-> JobRepository         : 13c. merge_output_files (Postgres)

' --- 5. Machine heartbeat (community only, continuous) ---
MachinesRouter       -[#2563eb]-> MachineService        : machine heartbeat
MachineService       -[#f97316]-> MachineHeartbeatRepository : ZADD machines:alive (Redis)

' --- 6. Success path: data triggers terminal transition ---
JobService           -[#f97316]-> CallbackRouter        : 14. notify_completion (BackgroundTask)\n     when count == total_frames
CallbackRouter       -[#0891b2]-> SuccessHandler        : 15. on SUCCESS outcome
SuccessHandler       -[#0891b2]-> RenderOrchestrator    : 16. on_job_succeeded
RenderOrchestrator   -[#7c3aed]-> RenderLifecycle       : 17. handle_chunk_succeeded
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed]-> JobRepository         : 18. mark_done
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed]-> LifecycleFramesDeduplication : 19. compute_total_rendered
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed]-> InProgressChunkRepository : 20. release ledger
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed]-> IFleetStrategy        : 21. eager cancel + stop_monitoring\n     (kills Vast / Modal immediately)
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed]-> MachineRepository     : 22. set_available (community lock release)
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed]-> RenderGroupRepository : 23. reconcile_group_status
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed]-> DispatchCoordinator   : 24. drain_for_fleet (sibling chunks)

' --- 7. Failure path: 5 sources, one router ---
JobsRouter           -[#2563eb]-> CallbackRouter        : F1a. agent_failure
InternalRouter       -[#2563eb]-> CallbackRouter        : F1b. /internal/orphan
VastInstanceMonitor  -[#16a34a,dashed]-> CallbackRouter : F1c. via _on_failure closure
ModalJobMonitor      -[#16a34a,dashed]-> CallbackRouter : F1d. via _on_failure closure
CommunityMonitor     -[#16a34a,dashed]-> CallbackRouter : F1e. via _on_failure closure

CallbackRouter       -[#0891b2]-> FailureHandler        : F2. on FAILURE outcome
FailureHandler       -[#0891b2]-> RenderOrchestrator    : F3. on_job_failed
RenderOrchestrator   -[#7c3aed]-> RenderLifecycle       : F4. handle_chunk_failed
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed]-> JobRepository         : F5. mark_failed
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed]-> LifecycleFramesDeduplication : F6. compute_remaining_for_chunk\n     (UNION across siblings)
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed]-> ChunkRequest          : F7. build retry request\n     (anti-affinity exclusions)
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed,bold]-> DispatchCoordinator   : F8. enqueue_and_flush(retry_task)\n     LOOPS BACK to step 6\n     (or terminal if retries exhausted)
note on link
  Loop terminates when:
    next_attempt > MAX_RETRIES
    OR allocate_retry returns None
    (no eligible target after exclusions)
  Either case -> reconcile_group_status,
  group may transition to 'failed'.
end note

' --- Stall-detection feeds the failure path (5th source) ---
VastInstanceMonitor  -[#16a34a,dashed]-> IPreRenderStallDetector : evaluates per tick\nin "running" block
ModalJobMonitor      -[#16a34a,dashed]-> IPreRenderStallDetector : evaluates per tick\nafter is_stale check
CommunityMonitor     -[#16a34a,dashed]-> IPreRenderStallDetector : evaluates per tick\nper running community job
IPreRenderStallDetector -[#a16207]-> HeartbeatRepository : reads sliding window\n(get_recent)
note on link
  StallReason -> monitor's _on_failure
  closure -> CallbackRouter (FAILURE)
  -> same retry path as steps F1..F8.
  Stall detection is the implicit
  pre-failure path: it just generates
  failure events from the worker's
  heartbeat stream when no other signal
  has fired yet (e.g. download wedged
  but heartbeats are still landing).
end note

' --- 8. Cancel path ---
RenderGroupsRouter   -[#2563eb]-> RenderGroupService    : C1. cancel
RenderGroupService   -[#f97316]-> RenderOrchestrator    : C2. cancel_group
RenderOrchestrator   -[#7c3aed]-> RenderLifecycle       : C3. cancel_render
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed]-> JobRepository         : C4. group + jobs -> 'cancelled'
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed]-> IFleetStrategy        : C5. cancel + stop_monitoring per job
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed]-> DispatchQueueRepository : C6. drain queue

' --- 9. Recovery (boot) ---
VastRecovery         -[#16a34a]-> VastCallbackHandler   : reattach in-flight monitors
ModalRecovery        -[#16a34a]-> ModalCallbackHandler  : reattach in-flight monitors

' --- Allocator's resource_picker reads liveness from Redis ---
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed]-> MachineRepository     : get_available_community\n(intersected w/ alive_ids)
RenderLifecycle      -[#7c3aed]-> MachineHeartbeatRepository : alive_ids snapshot

' --- Bootstrap wires the stall-detector factory into each fleet ---
VastCallbackHandler  -[#16a34a,dashed]-> PreRenderStallDetectorBuilder : factory injected,\n.build() per start_monitoring
ModalCallbackHandler -[#16a34a,dashed]-> PreRenderStallDetectorBuilder : factory injected,\n.build() per start_monitoring
CommunityMonitor     -[#16a34a,dashed]-> PreRenderStallDetectorBuilder : .build() ONCE at init\n(stateless across jobs)

' ============================================================
' Color legend
' ============================================================
legend right
  Arrow color = source module / layer
  ----
  blue    = API           (api/routers)
  orange  = Service       (services)
  violet  = Orchestration (orchestrator + lifecycle + dispatch)
  cyan    = Callbacks     (router + handlers)
  red     = Allocation    (strategies + validators)
  amber   = Stall Detection (detector + rules + builder)
  green   = Fleet         (registry + per-provider strategy / client / monitor / recovery)
  slate   = Repositories  (DB + Redis I/O)
  ----
  Numbered arrows = render lifecycle order (1..24)
  F-prefix = failure branch (F8 = explicit loop back to dispatch)
  C-prefix = cancel branch
end legend

@enduml
